Paisa Stick is a remote-like device designed to perform cashless transactions. It transfers value from the device to other types of devices like phones, IVRs, and Android apps.

Elderly members in society find it difficult to use digital payment interfaces. How might we enable them to perform daily transactions with ease?

The project won the [CHI 2017 Student Design Challenge](https://chi2017.acm.org/designcompetition.html) and the paper is published in the ACM Digital Library.
